cation-incompetent gene transfer vectors. Potential vaccines against feline infectious peritonitis will be developed by inserting sequences coding for immunogenic fragments of feline coronavirus (FCoV) S and M proteins into these vectors. Recombinant spumaviruses that look to be promising candidates as vaccines based on in vitro characteristics will be evaluated for their ability to express FCoV polypeptides in vivo and to stimulate an immune response to FCoV. If time allows, the ability of the recombinant(s) to prevent persistent infection of cats with FCoV will be evaluated.","plannedDates":[{"endDate":"2004-03-31T00:00:00+00:00","startDate":"2000-10-01T00:00:00+00:00"}],"amountAwarded":188500,"Financial Year":"2000/01","Lead Applicant":"Dr Allison C German","grantProgramme":[{"title":"Research Training Fellowship"}],"Applicant Surname":"German","Approval Committee":"Clinical Interest Group","fundingOrganization":[{"id":"GB-CHC-210183","name":"The Wellcome Trust"}],"recipientOrganization":[{"id":"360G-Wellcome-ORG:University-of-Bristol","name":"University of Bristol","addressCountry":"United Kingdom","addressLocality":"Bristol"}],"Has the grant transferred?":"No","Research conducted at multiple locations?":"No","Total amount including partnership funding":188500},"publisher":{"self":"https://api.threesixtygiving.org/api/v1/org/GB-CHC-210183/","org_id":"GB-CHC-210183"},"data_license":{"url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","name":"Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)"}},{"grant_id":"360G-Wellcome-061481_Z_00_Z","data":{"id":"360G-Wellcome-061481_Z_00_Z","title":"Is depression associated with an increased risk of recurrent foot ulcers in patients with diabetes?  ","Region":"London","currency":"GBP","awardDate":"2001-02-05T00:00:00+00:00","Internal ID":"061481/Z/00/Z","description":"No description available","plannedDates":[{"endDate":"2004-12-10T00:00:00+00:00","startDate":"2001-06-11T00:00:00+00:00"}],"amountAwarded":122333,"Fina